CM_ "BMW E90 ABS/DSC module (Continental MK60E1, DSC81, software ZB 6769845A). Node DSC = this module. Every frame of the firmware's two message tables is listed with every field: fields the firmware discards and transmitted fields with a fixed value are included and say so. The application is the M3 MK60E5 software with features removed: layouts and fixed or discarded fields are read from this image, while meanings, scalings and DTC numbers are carried over from the M3 firmware where the handler matches and are not verified separately here. Not checked against a bus capture. Byte/bit numbering 0-based, little-endian (Intel). Bus: F-CAN (chassis CAN, 500 kbit/s) to the steering-angle sensor and the yaw/acceleration sensor cluster.";
CM_ BO_ 128 "Commands from DSC to the sensor cluster and the steering-angle sensor (BMW: SYNC, DTC C99B on the receiving side): cluster self-test requests, steering-sensor calibration / coding commands, fault-memory clear and the cluster supply state. Field meanings as on the M3, whose routine that fills the frame is identical here. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 206 "The four wheel speeds, same content as PT-CAN 0x0CE (there every 20 ms). Signed: negative while the wheel direction is known and backward. Magnitude limited to 300 km/h. Sent by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 286 "Control interventions DSC -> active steering (AFS), 10 ms in the transmit table. The M3 firmware holds this record off; whether this image sends it was not checked. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 304 "Terminal (ignition) status: the PT-CAN 0x130 frame of the car access system, forwarded unchanged to F-CAN by the DSC as it is received (about every 100 ms). Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 884 "Learned wheel (tyre) tolerance trims, same content as PT-CAN 0x374. Sent by this module, every 1000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 195 "Not in the M3's table; sender and meaning not established. Received; every field is discarded and its timeout has no effect. Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 200 "Steering-angle sensor frame: angle, status, alive counter, angle rate and multiplexed service data. On this image it is the DSC's steering input (the M3 uses 0x0C9 for this) and the source of PT-CAN 0x0C4. No checksum; the alive counter is checked and the frame is supervised for timeout (DTC D373). Copies are forwarded to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 205 "Yaw/acceleration sensor cluster, channel set A: yaw rate, a supervision word and lateral acceleration, with status, alive counter and CRC-8. The source of yaw and ay. A repeated counter or bad CRC rejects the frame; supervised for timeout (DTC D370). Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 209 "Sensor cluster, channel set B: two supervision words and the longitudinal acceleration, with status, counter and CRC-8. Supervised for timeout (DTC D371). Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 212 "Sensor cluster status: status nibbles, status bytes and the flags with which the cluster answers the self-test requests of 0x080. Supervised for timeout (DTC D372). Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 280 "Active steering (AFS) -> DSC exchange (DTC D375). Received; every field is discarded and a timeout has no effect (the M3 has no active steering). Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 287 "Active steering (AFS) status (DTC D376). Received; every field is discarded and a timeout has no effect. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 320 "Sensor cluster identification: one 16-bit value, stored; reception marks the cluster as present. Received by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 404 "Cruise-control stalk. The DSC does not evaluate it; it forwards the frame unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, every 200 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 470 "Steering-wheel audio and telephone buttons. The DSC does not evaluate it; it forwards the frame unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, every 1000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 678 "Wiper switch. The byte is stored; the frame is also forwarded unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterYawTestRequest "1 while the yaw-rate self-test of the sensor cluster is requested; the cluster answers in 0x0D4.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterAccelTestRequest "1 while the acceleration self-test of the sensor cluster is requested; the cluster answers in 0x0D4.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterTestSpare "Always 0.";
CM_ SG_ 128 Spare_b4 "Always 0.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlCommand "Steering-sensor command while one is busy: 1 steering-angle calibration (KWP 31 21), 2 write the sensor's coding byte (KWP 2E 30 01). Held until the sensor reports it in 0x0C8 or 26 cycles.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlRoutine2F "2 while the steering-sensor routine 0x2F is requested (after an NM wake-up, a distance reset or a long standstill), otherwise 1.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlClearAll "Set for 5 frames after a full fault-memory clear (KWP 14 FF FF).";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlClearSlots "Set for 5 frames after the second fault-memory clear phase (KWP 14 FF FE).";
CM_ SG_ 128 Spare_b22 "Always 3.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterSupply "1 once the sensor cluster's supply is up and its start-up silence is over; 2 before that or with the supply low.";
CM_ SG_ 128 Spare_b26 "Always 0x3F.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlCommandArgument "Argument of SzlCommand: the calibration argument byte or the coding byte, otherwise 0.";
