CM_ SG_ 195 Field_b0 "Discarded.";
CM_ SG_ 195 Field_b16 "Discarded.";
CM_ SG_ 195 Field_b24 "Discarded.";
CM_ SG_ 200 SteerAngle "Steering wheel angle. The firmware rescales it by a constant / 1024 before use; 0.04395 deg per bit is the BMW figure.";
CM_ SG_ 200 SteerAngleStatus "Angle status: 0 and 1 are status classes, other values count as invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 200 AliveCounter "Alive counter. Checked.";
CM_ SG_ 200 SteerRate "Steering wheel angle rate, rescaled like the angle; becomes SteerRate on PT-CAN 0x0C4.";
CM_ SG_ 200 SensorState "Sensor state; the firmware keeps a flag for the value 1.";
CM_ SG_ 200 ServiceDataSelector "Selects what ServiceData carries. On the M3's 0x0C9: 0 and 1 sensor identity halves, 2 status, 3 fault code, 12 calibration byte; not checked selector by selector here.";
CM_ SG_ 200 ServiceData "Multiplexed service data, decoded by the same routine as the M3's.";
CM_ SG_ 205 YawRate "Yaw rate from the sensor cluster (word 0), 0.5e-4 rad/s per LSB (0.0028648 deg/s). The firmware multiplies it by a sign calibration of -1.";
CM_ SG_ 205 Word1 "Cluster word 1, stored but not used.";
CM_ SG_ 205 LateralAccel "Lateral acceleration from the sensor cluster (word 2), 0.001 g per LSB. The firmware multiplies it by a sign calibration of -1.";
CM_ SG_ 205 Status_A "2-bit status field (stored in the cluster status flags).";
CM_ SG_ 205 Status_B "2-bit status field (stored in the cluster status flags).";
CM_ SG_ 205 AliveCounter "Alive counter; a repeated value rejects the frame.";
CM_ SG_ 205 Checksum "CRC-8 of bytes 0-6 (poly 0x1D); mismatch -> message rejected.";
CM_ SG_ 209 Word3 "Cluster word 3 (second yaw channel), stored but not used as the yaw rate.";
CM_ SG_ 209 Word4 "Cluster word 4, stored but not used.";
CM_ SG_ 209 LongitudinalAccel "Longitudinal acceleration from the sensor cluster (word 5), 0.001 g per LSB with the stock scale calibration, no sign inversion.";
CM_ SG_ 209 Status_A "2-bit status field (stored in the cluster status flags).";
CM_ SG_ 209 Status_B "2-bit status field (stored in the cluster status flags).";
CM_ SG_ 209 AliveCounter "Alive counter; a repeated value rejects the frame.";
CM_ SG_ 209 Checksum "CRC-8 as 0x0CD.";
CM_ SG_ 212 Nibble0_lo "Cluster status nibble (stored).";
CM_ SG_ 212 Nibble0_hi "Cluster status nibble (stored).";
CM_ SG_ 212 Nibble1_lo "Cluster status nibble (stored).";
CM_ SG_ 212 Nibble1_hi "Cluster status nibble (stored).";
